          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "msrdi02zweqvql6y",
          "message": {
            "text": "DM-2140: A manual dispatch accepts an existing, validated release tag so a publish-stage infrastructure failure can be resumed without moving the immutable tag or cutting a fake patch release. Every checkout is pinned to RELEASE_REF; the workflow definition itself may come from main while package contents come from the original tag.",
            "markdown": "DM-2140: A manual dispatch accepts an existing, validated release tag so a publish-stage infrastructure failure can be resumed without moving the immutable tag or cutting a fake patch release. Every checkout is pinned to RELEASE_REF; the workflow definition itself may come from main while package contents come from the original tag."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/release.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 25,
                  "endLine": 42,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      release_ref:\n        description: Existing release tag to resume after an infrastructure failure\n        required: true\n        type: string\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: release-${{ inputs.release_ref || github.ref_name }}\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\nenv:\n  # Pinned to 22.21.0 — Node 22.22.2's setup-node toolcache ships a corrupt\n  # bundled npm (its `@npmcli/arborist` is missing `promise-retry`), which\n  # crashes any `npm install -g` before it can replace itself. Bumping back\n  # to a major-version range (`'22'`) is safe once 22.22.2 ages out.\n  NODE_VERSION: '22.21.0'\n  RELEASE_REF: ${{ inputs.release_ref || github.ref_name }}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ],
            "ext-ai-tool-confidence": 0.96
          },
          "rank": 90,
          "workItemUris": [
            "DM-2140"
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "prNoteAnchor/v1": "6978f589f36caaa2301366386fb5eb0e"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "msrdi0b8uoieqbyn",
          "message": {
            "text": "DM-2140: Pin npm 11.6.2 rather than npm@latest. Trusted publishing requires npm >=11.5.1, npm 11.6.2 supports the pinned Node 22.21.0, and a moving dist-tag can cross a Node engine boundary between otherwise identical release runs (npm 12.0.2 did exactly that).",
            "markdown": "DM-2140: Pin npm 11.6.2 rather than npm@latest. Trusted publishing requires npm >=11.5.1, npm 11.6.2 supports the pinned Node 22.21.0, and a moving dist-tag can cross a Node engine boundary between otherwise identical release runs (npm 12.0.2 did exactly that)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/release.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 171,
                  "endLine": 173,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      # Trusted publishing needs npm >= 11.5.1. Pin a known-compatible version:\n      # npm@latest can cross an engine boundary independently of NODE_VERSION.\n      - run: npm install -g npm@11.6.2"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
